# =============================================================================
# oc-deploy — fleet ship/poll/swap script (target-process-20260827.md).
#
# ONE script for the ship -> build -> deploy loop, run as a background task
# from the invoking agent (owner directive 2026-08-27 19:17Z: ship 2+3 and
# poll 8-17 are the SAME script; the agent launches it, the runtime injects
# the result). Replaces compiler dispatch+poll duties per staged plan:
#   S0 inert (plan-only) -> S1 shadow ship (dispatch live, swaps stay
#   compiler) -> S2 pilot swap -> S3 cutover (DONE 2026-08-28: compiler
#   retired; poll = THE deploy path; runbook = tools/archive/compiler.md archived).
#
#   oc-deploy ship [--sha <40-hex>] [--features <set>] [--execute]
#   oc-deploy poll [--execute]
#   oc-deploy swap-execute --sha <40-hex> --run <id> [--features F]
#                          [--artifact-dir D] [--drill]        # Phase B
#   oc-deploy watch [--with-delta]       # stray-commit tripwire (report-only)
#                                        # + optional upstream arithmetic leg
#   oc-deploy status [--json]            # read-only deployment / daemon state summary
#   (contributors RETIRED v0.4.91 — use oc-attrib --contributors)
#   oc-deploy fanout --run <id> [--dry-run]   # issue #24: mechanical notify fan-out
#   oc-deploy lineage-check [--prev P] [--sha S] [--repo R] [--json]
#                                        # read-only swap-guard verdict (v0.4.151)
#   oc-deploy recover-receipt [--journal J] [--run R] [--sha S] [--dry-run] [--historical] [--json]
#                                        # repair a truncated swap's missing ledger row (v0.4.153)
#                                        # v0.4.157: --run/--sha SELECT the journal they name.
#                                        # A selector matching nothing REFUSES (rc 2) — it never
#                                        # falls back to the newest journal (pre-v0.4.157 it did,
#                                        # and echoed the caller's run beside another run's journal).
#                                        # Several matches: the one still lacking a receipt step
#                                        # wins; still ambiguous -> rc 2, name one with --journal.
#                                        # repair a truncated swap's missing ledger row (v0.4.153)
#   oc-deploy --selftest
#
# S2 WIRING (2026-08-28, per s2-swap-journal-spec.md + owner tool-logging law):
#   - swap-execute = Phase B body. Runs under a systemd-run --user TRANSIENT
#     unit (spawned by init, not the opencrabs daemon) so the bounce it
#     triggers cannot kill its own verifier. poll --execute at S2 hands off
#     to that unit and exits BEFORE any bounce (Phase A/B split).
#   - JOURNAL: $STATE_DIR/oc-deploy/journal/swap-<short>-<epoch>-<pid>.jsonl —
#     append-only, one fsync'd JSON line per state-changing step BEFORE the
#     next step starts (auto-swap/backup/verify/install/seal/marker-write/
#     restart/post-verify/receipt/rollback). Last present line = last
#     completed step; a crash is reconstructable from the journal alone.
#   - MARKERS: deployed.sha + deployed.meta.json written by THIS script
#     between seal and restart (the 03:11Z gap: HQ had to hand-restore).
#     Rollback restores markers + baseline/orders backups too.
#   - LEDGER STAMP: every attempt (success OR rollback OR drill) ends with a
#     flock'd workers-ledger stamp kind=swap-result quoting the journal.
#   - AUTO-ROLLBACK: post-bounce verify fail = restore backup + restart +
#     re-verify + stamp ROLLED_BACK + A2A owner ping, automatic.
#   - NO CONSENT GATE (owner 2026-08-28 18:50Z: consent process ELIMINATED):
#     GREEN carrier run + artifact verify IS the authorization -> auto-swap.
#     Post-SMOKE-FAIL rollback stays the owner's call (no auto-rollback there);
#     the swap-chain auto-rollback on post-bounce verify fail is unchanged.
#
# LINEAGE GUARD (v0.4.148 ancestry; REBASE-AWARE v0.4.151):
#   swap-execute refuses to install an incoming sha that does not CARRY the
#   currently deployed change — that is what stops a stale/delayed build from
#   regressing the live binary. A fork-main rebase REWRITES shas and orphans
#   the deployed commit, so the v0.4.148 ancestry-only test refused EVERY
#   legitimate post-rewrite swap: fleet-blocking, reported 2026-09-12.
#   Verdicts:
#     monotonic — PREV is an ancestor of SHA -> accept (fast path, unchanged)
#     rewritten — PREV orphaned, but a commit in merge-base(PREV,SHA)..SHA has
#                 the SAME patch-id -> accept; journal reason
#                 rewrite-equivalent-swap + rewritten_twin
#     absent    — both objects exist and PREV's change is genuinely NOT carried
#                 -> refuse rc 2, journal non-monotonic-swap, stderr token
#                 OC_DEPLOY_SWAP_GUARD=stale-build
#     unknown   — either object missing from OC_DEPLOY_REPO -> guard SKIPPED
#                 (pre-v0.4.151 "if both exist" behaviour preserved)
#   POST-REWRITE LANE RUNBOOK: after a rebase, just re-run the oc-ship-chain
#   leg — the swap is accepted automatically as rewrite-equivalent-swap.
#   NEVER hand-edit deployed.sha to re-point around a refusal (that is exactly
#   the regression the guard exists to catch). Diagnose read-only with
#   `oc-deploy lineage-check [--prev P] [--sha S] [--repo R] [--json]`
#   (rc 0 monotonic|rewritten, rc 2 absent|unknown; prints verdict, twin and
#   next step). A deliberate, audited regression uses
#   `--allow-rewritten-lineage "<justification>" [--actor A]` — justification
#   is MANDATORY (bare flag -> rc 2, OC_DEPLOY_GATE=override-needs-justification)
#   and acceptance is journaled with justification + actor.
#
# RESTART SURVIVAL / CGROUP SAFETY (v0.4.153):
#   A DIRECT `swap-execute` inherits the cgroup of whoever launched it. When that
#   launcher is a session hosted by the very unit the swap bounces
#   (opencrabs-ops.service), step 8's `systemctl --user restart` tears the cgroup
#   down and SIGKILLs the swap AT the restart line. Steps 9-12 (post-verify,
#   sidecar-sync, receipt, fanout) never run, and because the swap-result ledger
#   stamp is deliberately LAST (v0.4.78 F-M1: receipt evidence must precede the
#   stamp, so a crash can never leave an unbacked DEPLOYED row) NO row is written
#   at all — the host is fully swapped and the ledger is SILENT. A false-negative
#   audit trail is the dangerous direction of error.
#   EVIDENCE 2026-09-12: journal swap-acb8e205-…jsonl stops at seq 7 marker-write
#   (mtime == swapped_at second; daemon restarted the SAME second), while
#   swap-74d85785-…jsonl — handed to a `systemd-run` transient unit by
#   `poll --execute`, i.e. OUTSIDE the unit — carries all 11 seqs.
#   FIX: swap-execute re-execs under a transient scope outside the bounce cgroup
#   BEFORE any work (pre-lock, so a re-entry can never self-deadlock on the held
#   host-swap.lock). The detach command MUST BLOCK and pass the child's rc
#   through (`systemd-run --user --scope`, `setsid -w`) — a non-blocking launcher
#   returns 0 immediately and a guard refusal would read as success.
#   RECOVERY: `oc-deploy recover-receipt` repairs the missing row for a swap that
#   already truncated. It stamps ONLY when the journal shows install exit=0 AND
#   marker-write exit=0, has NO receipt step, the sha resolves, and no existing
#   swap-result row quotes sha+run (idempotent — a re-run is a no-op). rc 0 =
#   handled (recovered, or correctly nothing to do) · rc 2 = refused (the journal
#   does not describe a recoverable real swap). `--historical` records a swap
#   whose sha was later SUPERSEDED instead of refusing; `--dry-run`/`--json`
#   inspect without writing. Fan-out is NOT replayed (use `oc-deploy fanout
#   --run <id>` — it has its own done-marker and a replay would re-notify).
#   Selftest section 22 covers this end-to-end with a restart shim that kills the
#   swap's own process group.
#
# HARD SAFETY RULES (v0.4.27 + S2):
#   - Plan-only UNLESS --execute. Every planned action prints as "PLAN: ...".
#     NEVER bare exit 0 — plan mode always prints its full delta.
#   - Kill file aborts EVERY invocation first (exit 9), selftest included.
#     Either $STATE_DIR/oc-deploy.kill or ${HOME:-/root}/oc-work/oc-deploy.disabled.
#   - Swap actions (poll execute + swap-execute) require stage >= S2.
#   - Consent gate RETIRED 2026-08-28 (owner order): GREEN run -> auto-swap.
#   - Shadow journal $STATE_DIR/oc-deploy-shadow.log records every run.
#   - Bash-only, seconds of runtime, zero cargo.
#
# Exit codes: 0 ok/noop | 1 usage | 2 rebase/gate/push/verify/rollback fail
#             / watch stray | 3 retired (was consent) | 4 stage gate / launch fail
#             | 5 poll --wait timeout (C-#2) | 9 kill file
# Deps: git, gh, jq, curl; oc-order-validate (ship execute);
#       oc-artifact-verify + oc-seal-state (swap-execute real mode)
# =============================================================================
